    >>> counts
    Array([[3, 0, 0],
           [1, 3, 0],
           [0, 1, 0]], dtype=int32)

    Using ``density=True`` returns a normalized histogram:

    >>> density, x_edges, y_edges = jnp.histogram2d(x, y, density=True)
    >>> dx = jnp.diff(x_edges)
    >>> dy = jnp.diff(y_edges)
